      "obligation": "refuter:3:1",
      "id": "lem-the-imprimitivity-reconstruction-map-is-isometric-and-intertwining",
      "location": "Proof 2.1",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The covariant-model definition says “F(xh)=σ(h)^{-1}F(x).” Proof 2.1 instead writes “F(g^{-1}s(x))=σ(h(g^{-1},x))F(s(g^{-1}x))” after expressing g^{-1}s(x)=s(g^{-1}x)h(g^{-1},x). Covariance gives σ(h(g^{-1},x))^{-1}; since h(g^{-1},x)=h(g,g^{-1}x)^{-1}, the factor matching the displayed induced action is σ(h(g,g^{-1}x)). The written equality has the inverse sign wrong; correcting it closes this local proof-step gap.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
